Let's start off with the initial information Jack received 200 invitees.He had hoped to have someone from every one show up so let's call the number of actual shows "x"and there isn't enough data yet but we know x= -c+e where c = the total responses given before any shows and e = the actual number of showings.Hence:*

$$
\begin{align*}
&x=\frac{ed}{c}\\ & 200-x= 0.8(200-x+\frac{ed}{c})-10\\ &400-2(x)= 0.8(400-2x)+d-10\\ &-x^{\prime \prime}=300-1.6x+d-10\\ &x^{\prime \prime}-\frac{x}{1.6}=d-2\\ \end{align*}
$$

Hence d would equal $\boxed{92}$.<|im_end|>

